    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag for owner responses.\n\n**Behavior:** `bulkSignupWarning` is `true` when **more than 80** owners already carry today's business day as their `registrationDate` (i.e. were \"created today\"), otherwise `false`. This reuses the exact accumulation path of the existing daily-registration-limit rule (owners counted by registration date), staying consistent with `toBusinessDay` handling.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` and an `isBulkSignupWarning()` helper, and set the flag on every returned `OwnerDto` (`addOwner`, `getOwner`, `updateOwner`, `listOwners`) so it's always explicitly `true`/`false` rather than null.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 marked `bulkSignupWarning` as `ignore = true` on `toOwnerDto` (it has no source property on the entity; the controller sets it), avoiding an unmapped-target warning.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`) \u2014 which creates a single fresh owner and asserts `$.bulkSignupWarning` is `false` via `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).",
